Helix H.264 encoder: frame setup and QP controls without rate control

With CONFIG_INGENIC_HELIX_H264E_RC_NONE (patch 0001) h264e_encode() never
built the slice header, the CABAC context or the VDMA descriptor of a
frame: the vendor does that inside the two rate-control variants
(h264e_rc_frame_start in librc, h264e_nl_rc_frame_start over netlink),
so the VPU was started on an empty descriptor and no frame came out.

This is the frame setup of the pre-rate-control helix/h264e.c of the
same SDK, which the Makefile no longer builds, moved into h264e_rc.c
behind the new choice. The QP of a frame is taken from the V4L2 controls
V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_H264_I_FRAME_QP (IDR slices) and
V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_H264_P_FRAME_QP (P slices), which helix_ops.c already
stores in p->i_qp and p->p_qp but nothing consumed; both default to 30,
the value the fixed i_global_qp had. The controls take effect on the
next frame, so a userspace rate controller can steer the bitrate.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor driver, project policy]

